                "senderName": "NWS Honolulu HI",
                "headline": "Flood Watch issued October 26 at 3:30PM HST until October 29 at 5:00AM HST by NWS Honolulu HI",
                "description": "A trough moving over the state from the southwest will bring\nabundant tropical moisture late Tuesday through at least Wednesday\nnight. Heavy rain and isolated thunderstorms are expected to produce\nflash flooding, and while the greatest flood threat will be focused\nover Oahu and Maui County, all islands are at risk.\n\n* WHAT...Flash flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...All main Hawaiian Islands.\n\n* WHEN...From Tuesday morning through late Wednesday night.\n\n* IMPACTS...Significant flooding may occur due to the overflow of\nstreams and drainages. Roads in several areas may be closed, along\nwith property damage in urban or low lying spots due to runoff.\nLandslides may also occur in areas with steep terrain.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Heavy showers and isolated thunderstorms with intense rain rates\nare expected to develop on Tuesday and continue through Wednesday\nnight as a trough moves over the state. While the greatest flood\nthreat will be focused over Oahu and Maui County, all islands are\nat risk.",
                "instruction": "You should monitor later forecasts and be prepared to take action\nshould Flash Flood Warnings be issued.",
                "response": "Prepare",
                "note": null,
